Subject: [experimental] Resample stay-warped copies into swapchain images

A texture left in a rate map's physical layout that is copied into an imported
(swapchain) image is drawn through the map's forward tables instead of copied
texel for texel, because the compositor reads that image outside DXMT. This is
how xrizer hands an OpenVR game's eye textures to OpenXR. Other whole-image
copies pass the layout on to their destination. Colour, single-sample sources
only; anything else is copied as before and warned about once.

Each copy into a swapchain image also leaves its source size and box on the
image as private data, so the OpenXR layer can fit the rate map to the texture
the application renders (both eyes in one texture, a render scale, part of a
larger texture) instead of to the swapchain. The copy shader is compiled from
source by winemetal when the prebuilt internal library does not have it.

